## A streamlined .gitignore for modern .NET projects
## including temporary files, build results, and
## files generated by popular .NET tools. If you are
## developing with Visual Studio, the VS .gitignore
## https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/VisualStudio.gitignore
## has more thorough IDE-specific entries.
##
## Get latest from https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Dotnet.gitignore

# Build results
[Dd]ebug/
[Dd]ebugPublic/
[Rr]elease/
[Rr]eleases/
x64/
x86/
[Ww][Ii][Nn]32/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]64/
bld/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/

# .NET Core
project.lock.json
project.fragment.lock.json
artifacts/

# ASP.NET Scaffolding
ScaffoldingReadMe.txt

# NuGet Packages
*.nupkg
# NuGet Symbol Packages
*.snupkg

# dotenv environment variables file
.env

# Others
~$*
*~
CodeCoverage/

# MSBuild Binary and Structured Log
*.binlog

# MSTest test Results
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
[Bb]uild[Ll]og.*

# NUnit
*.VisualState.xml
TestResult.xml
nunit-*.xml

# Rider
*.DotSettings.user

# Stray apphost symlink left in the working dir by running the DesktopClient
/SimplArchive.DesktopClient

# macos system files
.DS_Store

# Local backup output (scripts/backup.sh)
backups/

# Code-coverage output (CI + local `dotnet test --collect "XPlat Code Coverage"` + ReportGenerator)
coverage/

# Stryker.NET mutation-testing output (StrykerOutput/ is the default; stryker-out/ is the CI output path)
StrykerOutput/
stryker-out/

# macOS .dmg packaging output (scripts/package-macos-dmg.sh)
dist/

# Baked/staged desktop-client download artifacts (ADR 0490) — build outputs, not committed. The folder structure
# (.gitkeep) + clients/macos/index.html stay tracked; the Dockerfile / scripts/package-clients.sh produce these.
/src/SimplArchive.Api/wwwroot/download/clients/**/*.zip
/src/SimplArchive.Api/wwwroot/download/clients/**/*.tar.gz
/src/SimplArchive.Api/wwwroot/download/clients/**/*.dmg
white-bar-bug.png

# Screenshot debris and dropped fixtures at the repo root. `--demo` is what a malformed
# `--screenshot --demo` invocation writes when the flag order puts it where the output path belongs, and it
# reached the PUBLIC mirror twice before anyone noticed. Anything dropped here for verification (real scans,
# bug screenshots) is somebody's own document and must never be published.
/--*
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.png
src/SimplArchive.DesktopClient/--*

# Real scans dropped in the repo root for verification (#491). They are somebody's actual receipts and
# invoices, and this repository is published — so they must never be committed, not even by a sweeping
# `git add -A`, which is exactly how a set of them got committed once already.
/*.tif
/*.tiff

# Screenshots and scratch files dropped in ./tmp for a bug report. Same story as the scans above, and it has
# already happened once: a bug screenshot rode into `main` on a `git add -A` (#507) and had to be removed.
/tmp/

# Local-only connection settings + credentials for the private interop tooling (never committed)
tools/.local/

# Migration-run logs written by the private interop tooling (rolling JSON, ADR 0586)
logs/
